{"id": "test_hand2-036", "split": "test_hand2", "intent": "no_tool", "family": -1, "request": "what is the difference between RAM and storage?", "expected": null, "reply": "**RAM (Random\u2011Access Memory)** and **storage** serve two very different purposes in a computer, even though both hold data.\n\n| Aspect | RAM | Storage (e.g., SSD, HDD) |\n|--------|-----|--------------------------|\n| **Purpose** | Holds data that the CPU needs **immediately** while programs are running. | Holds data **long\u2011term**, keeping files, OS, applications, and other information even when the computer is powered off. |\n| **Volatility** | **Volatile** \u2013 loses its contents when power is removed. | **Non\u2011volatile** \u2013 retains data without power. |\n| **Speed** | Extremely fast (nanoseconds to microseconds). | Much slower (microseconds to milliseconds for SSDs; milliseconds for HDDs). |\n| **Typical Capacity** | Usually measured in gigabytes (GB) \u2013 e.g., 8\u202fGB, 16\u202fGB, 32\u202fGB. | Measured in gigabytes to terabytes (TB) \u2013 e.g., 256\u202fGB, 1\u202fTB, 4\u202fTB. |\n| **Cost per GB** | More expensive per gig", "call": null, "verdict": null, "score": {"called": false, "levels": null, "abstained_ok": true, "error": null}}
